  "chapter": "Reservations",
  "codeGen": {},
  "notes": [
    "## Event to field reasoning - Active Reservations\n\n- **Reservation Placed** -> sets `Email`, `Code`, `Start`, `End`, `NumberOfPeople` - the row's creation event. A reservation does not exist in this projection before it.\n\nThat is the only inbound event on **this instance**. Cancellation is handled by the linked copy in column G, not by an edge back into this node - see that column's note.\n\n### Why `Id` is not projected here\n\nThis screen is read-only: the guest looks at the list, it issues no command. Nothing on it needs a reservation's identity, so `Id` is deliberately left out rather than carried speculatively. The `Reservation By Code` read model in column E does project `Id`, because its screen issues `Cancel Reservation`.\n\n### Fan-in\n\nOne source event. Well under the >3-events threshold - no split needed, nothing to justify."
